{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1iteUzvyLetntwCf8iv", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LJ526PiPGfowra13SZEyaX", "name": "mcp__device__sign_off", "input": {"confidence": 0.6, "verdict": "PASS", "notes": "Tested: copy/paste with conflicts (Do for all with Skip, a second paste starting unchecked, Rename, Overwrite), renaming a file with \"+\" in its name, sort by size descending (kept across folders), grid/list toggle, adding bookmarks including a duplicate and a same-title/different-path entry, and the SMB dialog Anonymous toggle. One report filed: after creating an anonymous SMB connection, the edit dialog shows Anonymous checked but the username and password fields are not disabled. The developer could not reproduce it from my steps, though I saw it twice. I also saw the folder header read \"0 folders and 0 files\" once, on Alpha, while its list had 1 folder and 1 file; it showed the right count when I re-entered the folder, so I did not report it. Not covered: sort by Last Modified and Type, the \"Only this folder\" sort option, the History and Hidden Files options, rotating during a paste, and deleting a bookmark."}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1016, "cache_read_input_tokens": 125117, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1016}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "2e715b82-cd69-46b0-82c4-b614b937bec4", "uuid": "3bcfc184-dd0b-49fb-819a-71c0521b7f6e", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T22:33:46.122Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1iteCQ95Yjcqfmu6kL1", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01LJ526PiPGfowra13SZEyaX": {"confidence": 0.6, "verdict": "PASS", "notes": "Tested: copy/paste with conflicts (Do for all with Skip, a second paste starting unchecked, Rename, Overwrite), renaming a file with \"+\" in its name, sort by size descending (kept across folders), grid/list toggle, adding bookmarks including a duplicate and a same-title/different-path entry, and the SMB dialog Anonymous toggle. One report filed: after creating an anonymous SMB connection, the edit dialog shows Anonymous checked but the username and password fields are not disabled. The developer could not reproduce it from my steps, though I saw it twice. I also saw the folder header read \"0 folders and 0 files\" once, on Alpha, while its list had 1 folder and 1 file; it showed the right count when I re-entered the folder, so I did not report it. Not covered: sort by Last Modified and Type, the \"Only this folder\" sort option, the History and Hidden Files options, rotating during a paste, and deleting a bookmark."}}, "tool_use_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01LJ526PiPGfowra13SZEyaX", "display_name": "Sign Off", "server_display_name": "aqb-device", "tool_name": "sign_off"}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01LJ526PiPGfowra13SZEyaX", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Signed off. The session has ended."}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "2e715b82-cd69-46b0-82c4-b614b937bec4", "uuid": "ab488b0d-a0af-4779-bd08-6223edc2a538", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T22:33:46.127Z", "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01LJ526PiPGfowra13SZEyaX", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1iu3U7aDJMcegPWCwoV", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with a PASS at 0.6 confidence. I filed one bug report and the developer rejected it as not reproducible.\n\n**What I tested, and what worked**\n- **Paste conflicts:** \"Do for all items\" with Skip applied to the remaining conflicts of that paste. A second paste started with the box unchecked. Rename produced `keep (1).jpg`, and Overwrite worked.\n- **Renaming:** `report+final.txt` renamed to `report final v2.txt` and showed correctly in the list.\n- **Sorting and view:** Size descending gave the right order and held in other folders. The grid and list toggle both worked.\n- **Bookmarks:** Alpha and Beta were added. Adding Alpha again did not duplicate it. A second \"Beta\" at a different path (`Alpha/Beta`) was added correctly.\n- **SMB dialog:** Ticking Anonymous greys out the username and password fields, and unticking restores them. A new connection, TestSMB, was created and appeared in the drawer.\n\n**The report that was rejected**\nWhen I reopened the saved TestSMB connection to edit it, Anonymous was ticked but the username and password fields were not disabled. I saw this twice. I filed it twice and the developer replied \"could not reproduce with the steps given\" both times. It may be real.\n\n**One glitch I didn't report**\nOnce the Alpha folder header read \"0 folders and 0 files\" while the list showed 1 folder and 1 file. It showed the right count when I re-entered the folder, and I couldn't make it happen again.\n\n**Not covered**\n- Sort by Last Modified and by Type\n- The \"Only this folder\" sort option\n- History and Hidden Files\n- Rotating during a paste\n- Deleting a bookmark\n\nI also changed some data: I copied files and folders into Beta and Alpha, renamed a file, and added three bookmarks and the TestSMB connection."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 587, "cache_read_input_tokens": 126133, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 587}, "output_tokens": 626, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "2e715b82-cd69-46b0-82c4-b614b937bec4", "uuid": "b6d41846-3336-4475-a463-aa859943d65f", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T22:33:51.666Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1iu3EVCnBvrwUgK5T7w"}
